{"ready":true,"data":{"id":"daniel-br-hl","name":"Daniel Brühl","birthDate":"1978-06-16","birthPlace":" Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain","bio":"Daniel César Martín Brühl González (German: [ˈdaːni̯eːl ˈbʁyːl, -ni̯ɛl -]; Spanish: [daˈnjel ˈbɾul ɡonˈθaleθ]; born 16 June 1978) is a German-Spanish actor. He has received various accolades, including three European Film Awards and three German Film Awards, along with nominations for two Golden Globe Awards and a BAFTA Award. He received his first German Film Award for Best Actor for his roles in Das Weisse Rauschen (2001), Nichts Bereuen (2001), and Vaya con Dios (2002). His starring role in the German film Good Bye, Lenin! (2003) received widespread recognition and critical acclaim, and garnered him the European Film Award for Best Actor and another German Film Award for Best Actor.\n\nHe was introduced to mainstream international audiences through his breakthrough performance as Fredrick Zoller, a Nazi German war hero in Quentin Tarantino's Inglourious Basterds (2009), and appearances in films like The Bourne Ultimatum (2007), The Fifth Estate (2013), and A Most Wanted Man (2014). Brühl received widespread critical acclaim and further recognition for his portrayal of former Formula 1 driver Niki Lauda in the biographical film Rush (2013), for which he earned nominations including the Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor, the Critic's Choice Award for Best Supporting Actor, the Screen Actors Guild Award for Best Supporting Actor and the BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Supporting Role.\n\nIn the Marvel Cinematic Universe, Brühl portrays Helmut Zemo in Captain America: Civil War (2016) and the Disney+ series The Falcon and the Winter Soldier (2021). He also starred as Dr. Laszlo Kreizler in the Emmy- and Golden Globe-nominated period drama television series The Alienist (2018–2020), for which he earned a nomination for the Golden Globe Award as Best Actor in a Television Motion Picture at the 76th Golden Globe Awards in 2018.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Daniel Brühl, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.","source":"TMDB","fetchedAt":"2026-11-19T17:41:09+00:00","tmdbId":3872,"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/person/3872","credits":[{"id":"civil-war","title":"Captain America: Civil War","character":"Zemo"},{"id":"falcon","title":"The Falcon and the Winter Soldier","character":"Baron Zemo"}],"photo":"./public-data/images/people/daniel-br-hl.webp","filmography":[{"name":"The Gallerist","year":2026,"character":"","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/mEi0c3wUrjnekhv02RM1kEAC3Qc.jpg"},{"name":"Eden","year":2025,"character":"Heinz","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/jbFEESMVbpJU8IjZBjiWGJdEsxR.jpg"},{"name":"Berlin Hero","year":2025,"character":"Alex Allonge","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/o83t6sTDBqN5hhUZZW4uUJNbWEg.jpg"},{"name":"Karl - Der Mann hinter der Maske","year":2025,"character":"Self","mediaType":"movie","poster":""},{"name":"Race for Glory: Audi vs. Lancia","year":2024,"character":"Roland Gumpert","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ovoybG8mCn6nQ6i5WoC8DdR08c2.jpg"},{"name":"The Franchise","year":2024,"character":"Eric Bouchard","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kWitzLQnweAcYFyjzVblkoByQDO.jpg"},{"name":"Becoming Karl Lagerfeld","year":2024,"character":"Karl Lagerfeld","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tfaRjAqNpDj5zngrReu6YbebrzO.jpg"},{"name":"Daniel Brühl: Breaking Bad","year":2023,"character":"Self - Actor","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kxwtTdHquKObHiT8LAWsHDQricj.jpg"},{"name":"The Movie Teller","year":2023,"character":"Hauser","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/w1TGEhGbcvIp0MnUGdzDdTji9E9.jpg"},{"name":"Making All Quiet on the Western Front","year":2022,"character":"Self","mediaType":"movie","poster":"http